  "source": "syensqo-galden-ht",
  "page": 2,
  "summary": "Perfluoropolyether (PFPE) heat-transfer fluids in nine boiling-point grades from 55 °C to 270 °C. Syensqo lists the same thermal conductivity (0.065 W/m·K) and dielectric strength (40 kV, 2.54 mm gap) for every grade and states there are no flash or fire points. Its listed uses include semiconductor, vapour-phase heating, recirculating chillers, and transformer and supercomputer cooling. All values at 25 °C unless stated.",
  "pfas": {
    "status": "pfas",
    "basis": "structure",
    "quote": "Galden® HT PFPE fluids do not contain hydrogen in their chemical structure",
    "page": 2,
    "note": "A perfluoropolyether is fully fluorinated, so it meets the OECD (2021) structural definition of PFAS."
  },
